# Sign-in, registration, proof of work, recovery code, terms acceptance, password reset, and reauth.

terms-version = Version { $version }, updated { $date }.
signin-title = Sign in
signin-lead = Your Baylee account, for online tables, contacts and the chat.
signin-name = Sign-in name
signin-password = Password
signin-submit = Sign in
signin-missing = Enter your sign-in name and password.
signin-working = Securing your password … this takes a moment and happens only in your browser.
signin-wrong = That sign-in name and password do not match. Check both and try again.
signin-failed-title = Sign-in failed
signin-failed-hint = You can try again right away, or use “Forgot your password?” to request a new password.
signin-not-moved = This account has not moved to Baylee Central yet. Sign in once with the Baylee client to move your account.
signin-no-account = No account yet? <register>Create one</register>.
signin-forgot = Forgot your password? <reset>Set a new one with a reset code</reset>.
register-have-account = Already have an account? <signin>Sign in</signin>.
signin-noscript = Signing in needs JavaScript: your password is processed in your browser and never sent to us.
register-title = Create an account
register-lead = For online tables, contacts and the chat. Free and open to everyone in the open beta.
register-name = Sign-in name
register-name-hint = Private, only for signing in: 3 to 24 lowercase letters, digits, dots, dashes or underscores.
register-display = Display name
register-display-hint = How other players see you: 3 to 16 letters, digits, - and _. Your tag is drawn for you.
register-password = Password
register-password-hint = At least 8 characters. A long sentence is easy to remember and hard to guess.
register-repeat = Repeat password
register-repeat-hint = The same once more, to catch a typo.
register-age = I am 13 or older.
register-consent = I accept the <terms>terms of use</terms>. How we handle your data is in the <privacy>privacy notice</privacy>.
register-submit = Create account
register-error-name = The sign-in name needs 3 to 24 lowercase letters, digits, dots, dashes or underscores.
register-error-display = The display name needs 3 to 16 letters or digits, with - and _ only inside.
register-error-reserved = This display name is reserved. Choose another.
register-error-short = The password needs at least 8 characters.
register-error-long = The password is too long.
register-error-repeat = The two passwords are not the same.
register-error-age = You need to be 13 or older to have an account.
register-error-consent = Accept the terms of use to create an account.
register-error-taken = This sign-in name is taken. Choose another.
code-title = Your recovery code
code-lead = Only with this code does your encrypted data survive if you forget your password. We do not know it and cannot restore it. Keep it somewhere safe where you will find it even without this device.
code-shown-once = Shown only now
code-download = Save as a text file
code-kept = I have saved my recovery code
code-not-kept = Save the code first, then confirm it.
code-continue = Continue
code-later = Not now
code-copy = Copy
code-copied = Copied.
code-copy-tooltip = Copy recovery code
code-copied-tooltip = Recovery code copied
code-copy-failed = Copying did not work here. Select the code and copy it by hand.
code-print = Print
code-manager = Save in password manager
code-manager-id = Baylee recovery code ({ $name })
code-manager-offered = Your browser was offered the code. If it asked you, check that it saved it.
code-manager-failed = Your browser did not take the code. Keep it another way.
code-mail = Mail it to myself
code-mail-warning = Careful: the code then lies in your mailbox. Whoever can read your mail can also have a reset code sent there, and with both reset your sign-in and open your encrypted data.
code-mail-subject = My Baylee recovery code
code-sheet-title = Baylee recovery code
code-sheet-name = Sign-in name: { $name }
code-sheet-what = With this code your encrypted Baylee data survives a forgotten password: you enter it on the reset page, together with a reset code.
code-sheet-keep = Keep it where only you can reach it. Nobody at Baylee will ever ask you for it.
code-email-label = E-mail address (optional)
code-email-hint = For a reset code if you forget your password. After this step we mail a code to confirm the address. You can also add one later in your account.
code-email-step-title = Confirm your e-mail address
code-email-step-lead = Enter the code from the mail here, or later on your account's security page.
code-email-step-done = Continue to your account
reset-title = Set a new password
reset-lead = For when you forgot your password: with a reset code you set a new one here. The code comes by e-mail to your confirmed address, or from an administrator.
reset-noscript = Setting a new password needs JavaScript: your password and your recovery code are processed in your browser and never sent to us.
reset-code = Reset code
reset-code-hint = By e-mail or from an administrator. It starts with RESET and works once: for one hour if it came by e-mail, for 24 hours if an administrator made it.
reset-data = Your encrypted data
reset-keep = I have my recovery code. My data stays.
reset-new = I do not have it. Start with an empty vault.
reset-recovery = Recovery code
reset-recovery-hint = The code you saved when you created your account. It stays in your browser and is never sent to us.
reset-warning = With an empty vault your encrypted data is lost for good: the settings saved in your account, your deck backups and your chat history. Nobody can bring it back, and neither can we. Your account, your display name and your contacts stay. You get a new recovery code.
reset-warning-confirm = I understand that this data is lost for good.
reset-submit = Set new password
reset-missing = Enter your sign-in name, the reset code and a new password.
reset-recovery-missing = Enter your recovery code, or choose the empty vault.
reset-error-code = That is not a reset code. It starts with RESET, followed by eight groups of four characters.
reset-error-recovery = This recovery code does not open your account's data. Check it and try again. Nothing was changed, and your reset code still works.
reset-error-confirm = Confirm first that you know what is lost.
reset-refused = This sign-in name and reset code do not go together, or the code has expired or was used already. Check both. If nothing helps, ask for a new code.
reset-done-title = Your new password is set
reset-done-kept = Your data and your recovery code stay as they were. You are signed out everywhere. Sign in with your new password.
reset-done-new = You start with an empty vault and are signed out everywhere. Below is your new recovery code — the old one no longer works.
reset-unsure-title = No answer came back
reset-unsure = The connection broke before Baylee Central answered, so we cannot tell whether your new password was set. Try to sign in with it. If that fails, nothing was changed: your reset code still works, enter it here again.
reset-unsure-code = If your new password works, this is your new recovery code and the old one no longer works. It cannot be shown again, so save it now. If your new password does not work, this code is worth nothing.
reset-to-signin = Sign in
reset-mail-title = No reset code?
reset-mail-lead = Enter your sign-in name. If your account has a confirmed e-mail address, we send a reset code to it.
reset-mail-name-hint = The name you sign in with, not your e-mail address.
reset-mail-submit = Send a code by e-mail
reset-mail-error-name = That is not a sign-in name. Enter the name you sign in with, not your e-mail address.
reset-mail-sent = If this account has a confirmed e-mail address, a reset code is on its way to it. It is valid for one hour.
reset-mail-busy = Too many requests for now. Try again later.
reset-mail-none = This server sends no mail. Ask an administrator for a reset code.
reset-mail-early = That was too quick. Try again in a moment.
terms-step-title = New terms of use
terms-step-lead = Baylee Central's terms changed. Read them and accept them to use your account, or decline and sign out.
terms-accept = Accept
terms-decline = Decline and sign out
reauth-lead = This needs a recent sign-in. Enter your sign-in name and password once more.
reauth-submit = Sign in again
register-closed = Registration is paused right now. Try again later.
register-refused = The registration was not accepted. Try again.
register-solving = Your browser is solving a puzzle that keeps robots out. When many accounts are being created, this can take a few minutes … { $percent } %
code-created = Account created
code-handle-label = Your handle
code-keep-title = Keep it now, in at least one of these ways
code-mail-opened = Your mail program should open now with a draft. If nothing happens, this browser has none set up: keep the code another way.
terms-step-version = Version { $version }
terms-read-hint = Read the text to its end, then you can accept.
terms-read-done = Read to the end.
keep-zip-pw-label = ZIP password (optional)
keep-zip-pw-placeholder = Encrypt attachment with a password
keep-zip-pw-warn = Without a password, the ZIP archive will be sent unencrypted.
keep-mail-send-error = Could not send the backup email. Check your address and try again.
register-invite-code = Invite code (optional)
register-invite-code-required = Invite code
register-invite-code-hint = Have a friend invite? Enter the code here.
register-invite-invalid = This invite code is invalid, expired, or has already been used.
